{#-
  The C-ABI install seam every Rust component exports (`nros::node!`), declared
  once for both C++ entries (the board entry and the PX4 module entry).

  Issue 2568 -- `params` / `n_params` are the node's launch `<param>` initials,
  a flat `[name0, value0, name1, value1, ...]` C-string array (`nullptr, 0`
  when it has none); `node_body.jinja` writes the call. The seam used to carry
  only `(node, executor, self)`, so a Rust node in a C++ entry read every
  `ctx.param(name)` as unset. The array is read during the call only.

  What the caller puts in scope: `rust_pkgs`, the Rust components.
-#}
extern "C" {
{%- for c in rust_pkgs %}
    int32_t __nros_component_{{ c.pkg | pkg_ident }}_install(const void* node, void* executor, void* self, const char* const* params, size_t n_params);
{%- endfor %}
}
